{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.star","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L277-L341","doc":"**The (★) identity** at every order `n` (stated; machine-exactly\nverified for n ≤ 32 as integer-Laurent dict equality, and numerically\nto 1e-497 for n ≤ 64). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:habiro-tail-star-identity","label":"prop:habiro-tail-star-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/habiro-tail-star-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.masbaumC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.masbaumC","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L268-L275","doc":"The exact Masbaum coefficient `C_{5₂,n}(a)` (integer Laurent in `a`;\nDOI 10.2140/agt.2003.3.537), transcribed from the merged compute:\n`C_n(a) = (−1)ⁿ Σ_k a^{3n²+5n+k²−2k−3nk} · a^{−k(n−k)}·[n,k]_{a²}` —\nstated with ℤ-exponents via `zpow`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch_sq_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch_sq_inv","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L263-L266","doc":"Literal-`q⁻¹` form of `qPoch_sq_inv'`, for `q ≠ 0` in a field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_inv","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L256-L261","doc":"Literal-`q⁻¹` form of `gaussBinom_inv'`, for `q ≠ 0` in a field. The\nmathematical content is the division-free lemma; this is the shape the\nMasbaum transform and the downstream corollaries consume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch_sq_inv'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch_sq_inv'","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L225-L248","doc":"**Bar-inversion of the squared Pochhammer**, division-free:\n`(q;q)_n² = q^{n(n+1)}·(qi;qi)_n²` whenever `q * qi = 1`. (The unsquared\nform carries a `(−1)ⁿ` and the half-exponent `n(n+1)/2`; squaring clears\nboth, and the square is what (★) needs.) The literal `q⁻¹` form is\n`qPoch_sq_inv` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.qPoch","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L222-L223","doc":"`(q;q)_n = ∏_{j=1..n} (1 − q^j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_inv'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_inv'","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L173-L220","doc":"**Bar-inversion** (the heart of (★)), division-free over a generic\n`CommRing`: whenever `qi` is a two-sided inverse of `q` (`hq : q * qi = 1`),\n`[n,k]_q = q^{k(n−k)}·[n,k]_{qi}`, unconditional (both sides vanish for\n`k > n`). This is the lemma that collapses the quadratic exponents of the\nMasbaum transform, and it needs no field — only the unit witness, so it\nholds verbatim over `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. The literal `q⁻¹` form is\n`gaussBinom_inv` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_succ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_succ'","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L120-L171","doc":"The dual Pascal rule\n`[n+1,k+1]_q = q^{n−k}·[n,k]_q + [n,k+1]_q`, unconditional (for\n`k > n` every term vanishes and truncated subtraction is harmless) —\nproved by induction from the primary recurrence alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L115-L118","doc":"`[n,0]_q = 1` for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_self","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L105-L113","doc":"`[n,n]_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_eq_zero_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_eq_zero_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L87-L103","doc":"`[n,k]_q = 0` for `k > n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_succ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L80-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero_succ","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L77-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom_zero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.gaussBinom","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailStar.lean#L66-L73","doc":"Gaussian binomial `[n,k]_q` by the Pascal recurrence\n`[n+1,k+1]_q = [n,k]_q + q^{k+1}·[n,k+1]_q` (the same recurrence the\nexact compute uses). ","signatureChunk":0}]}